# ◈ packages.xorg.list — mainline Xorg + suckless desktop
#
# Alternative to packages.xlibre.list (see that file for why they're
# separate rather than combined — XLibre and Xorg cannot coexist on the
# same installed system, so both are built and published, and the choice
# of which to actually install is left to whoever's consuming the binhost).
#
# This is the safe, mainline option: x11-base/xorg-server lives in
# Gentoo's main tree, unlike XLibre which needs a third-party overlay.
#
# media-libs/mesa is not listed explicitly here — it'll get pulled in
# automatically with +X once xorg-server needs it, resolved via the same
# --autounmask-write=y in build-binpkg.py already used elsewhere. This is
# a different matrix job/container than packages.graphics.list (which
# builds mesa with -X for the Wayland stack), so there's no conflict
# between the two mesa builds — they simply never coexist in the same
# container.
#
# xinit is included so X can actually be started (`startx`) rather than
# just installed.

x11-base/xorg-server
x11-apps/xinit
x11-drivers/xf86-input-libinput

x11-wm/dwm
x11-terms/st
x11-misc/dmenu
